  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Task: An **n-bit gray code sequence** is a sequence of `2n` integers where:\n\n* Every integer is in the **inclusive** range `[0, 2n - 1]`,\n* The first integer is `0`,\n* An integer appears **no more than once** in the sequence,\n* The binary representation of every pair of **adjacent** integers differs by **exactly one bit**, and\n* The binary representation of the **first** and **last** integers differs by **exactly one bit**.\n\nYou receive an integer `n`, output *any valid **n-bit gray code sequence***.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "n = 2",
        "output": "[0,1,3,2]",
        "explanation": "For this input, applying the required rules of Gray Code produces [0,1,3,2]."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "n = 1",
        "output": "[0,1]",
        "explanation": "For this input, applying the required rules of Gray Code produces [0,1]."
      }
    ],
    "notes": []
